{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you shall cook and eat.</b> It uses the language of cooking, whereas the Torah said regarding the commandment of the Paschal lamb (Exodus 12:9) ״אַל תֹּאכְלוּ וְגוֹ׳ וּבָשֵׁל מְבֻשָּׁל״. Perhaps it refers back to the slaughter of cattle for peace-offerings, of which the verse said above ״וְזָבַחְתָּ פֶּסַח צֹאן וּבָקָר״ and so forth, and our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Pesachim 70a): sheep for the Paschal lamb and cattle for peace-offerings. And in my work Pri To'ar on Yoreh De'ah I elaborated on this matter at the beginning of siman 87."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The closing quotation from Exodus 12:9 is given as a fragment with וגו׳ and rendered accordingly; the full verse continues מְבֻשָּׁל מְבֻשָּׁל בַּמָּיִם כִּי אִם צְלִי אֵשׁ."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:37.687487125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}